;Notes:
* Players should use the best weapons they can for damage, and their best power armour.
* The [[noxious scythe]], [[Masuta's warspear]] and [[Dragon Rider lance]] are far superior to other melee options due to their increased attack range and synergy with area of effect abilities.
** [[Laniakea's spear]] is an alternative option on tasks where its accuracy is not a hindrance due to its unique passive effect, which can pair with cinderbane gloves and [[weapon poison+++]], and its increased attack range.
* [[Cinderbane gloves]] are extremely useful against monsters that are not immune to [[poison]], as they apply a poisonous effect to all monsters the player is in combat with.
* [[Ring of vigour]] is not needed to be equipped after combined with [[warped gem]], a reward from completion of [[Extinction]] quest.

===Slayer helmet===
[[File:Corrupted slayer helmet chathead.png|left|50px]]
The most essential piece of gear is the [[slayer helmet]] and its variants. It provides a 7.5-9.5% increase to damage and 12.5-14.5% increase to accuracy when slaying monsters on-task and incorporates all slayer headgear effects, including [[spiny helmet]], [[face mask]], [[earmuffs]], [[nose peg]].

Maximum of 5 fully charged [[ring of slaying]] and 6 fully charged [[ferocious ring]]s can be stored in the slayer helmets with 60 [[Crafting]] and unlocking the ability for 500 [[Slayer point]]s.

All slayer helmets can be stored on the [[slayer helmet stand]] in [[Anachronia base camp]], granting its on-task damage and accuracy boost as a passive effect, allowing players to wear any style specific helmet. Ring of slaying and ferocious ring effects do not work with the helmet on the stand.
{{Slayer helmet upgrades}}

===Cannons===
A [[cannons|cannon]] is another incredibly useful piece of equipment, which is often used to speed up tasks. The "Restocking Cannon" perk purchased from the [[Artisans' Workshop Reward Shop]] with 100 [[Respect (Artisans' Workshop)|respect]] (with 150 extra in the upgrade progress) is quite essential to reduce the effort to maintain the cannons. The [[dwarf multicannon]] and [[kinetic cyclone]] are the [[Ranged]] and [[Melee]] variant of the cannons respectively. The [[Oldak coil]] is a [[Magic]] variant which is further recommended to be used instead of the dwarf multicannon, if possible.

Unlocking the [[dwarf multicannon upgrade kit|dwarf multicannon]], [[kinetic cyclone upgrade kit|kinetic cyclone]], and [[Oldak coil upgrade kit]]s can permanently increase their damage output by 100%, 50%, and 50% respectively.

These are incredibly useful for [[Dark beasts (Slayer assignment)|dark beast]] and [[Edimmu (Slayer assignment)|edimmu assignment]]s, as they constantly cycle aggression towards the player whenever they are hit. Most tasks can generally be completed within the duration of the cannon (25 minutes), and even then maintenance is fairly low if it runs out of [[cannonballs]], with a simple click to get it back up and running again. Some areas will prohibit the use of these cannons, so [[aggression potion]]s should be used in their place if necessary.

===Perks===
{{See also|Optimal PvM perk setup}}
Any [[perks]] that increase damage output is beneficial while slaying monsters. The perks shown in the table below are specifically useful for Slayer. [[Scavenging]] is arguably the best perk for Slayer and should be prioritised.
