==Slayer Codex and Sunken Pyramid==
Players with at least level 99 Slayer can fill their [[Slayer Codex]]. It is advised to invest [[slayer points]] and time to collect at least 100 different monster souls. For every 20 souls collected, [[slayer helmet]]s grant a +1% gain (up to 5% at 100 souls) to Slayer experience, effectively being an [[Experience-boosting set#Regular experience-boosting items|experience boosting item]].

In addition to the Slayer Codex, players with at least 99 Slayer have access to a [[Sunken Pyramid]]. The following slayer assignments are recommended to fill the three rooms available, or a player can access another player's dungeon if they have a needed room setup.

{| class="wikitable"
! Assignment
! Reason
! Recommended amount of spawns
|-
| [[Muspah]]
| Two additional spawns (the Cradle only possesses three somewhat slow spawns). Place in the small room.
| 5
|-
| [[Ripper Demon]]s
| With only 1 Ripper Demon, it removes the <35% player's life points [[aggression]] mechanic, meaning that no other demons will become aggressive towards the player when health drops below 35%. This also allows for safe use of [[Aoe abilities|AoE abilities]]. A lone ripper demon can also be found just south of the Mage Arena and is quite safe.
| 1
|-
| [[Crystal Shapeshifter]]s
| Easier grouping and use of AoE abilities. Place in the small room.
| 5
|-
| [[Shadow creature]]s
| Easier time attacking multiple shadows at once and use of AoE. Best to put Manifest Shadows in your dungeon as they are greater experience/kill than other shadow creatures. Place in the small room.
| 5
|-
| [[Hydrix dragon]]s
| Easily AFKable by standing under the spawn point, as the dragon uses relatively weak melee and magic attacks that can be easily healed off of via Soul Split.
| 1
|}

